Danger – Episode 1: The Spark of Chaos

Scene 1 | The Calm Before the Storm
Interior – High School Science Lab – Evening

The lab is dimly lit. Shadows stretch across cluttered workbenches stacked with beakers, test tubes, and half-finished experiments. A faint hum of fluorescent lights mixes with the occasional bubble from a glowing chemical solution. Dust floats lazily in the air, caught in the pale beams cutting through the blinds.

Jack, a tall, lanky teenager with glasses slipping down his nose, carefully pours a luminescent green liquid into a beaker. Beside him, Monica, meticulous and precise, adjusts a dial on a small, humming contraption that looks far more advanced than the rest of the lab.

Monica: (whispering) “Jack, slow down. If we overheat it again, we’ll get another… incident.”

Jack: (grinning) “Relax, Monica. This time, I’ve calculated everything down to the microsecond. It’s perfect.”

In the background, Mike and Jolly watch silently. Mike leans against a counter, arms crossed, bored, while Jolly fiddles with a small device, his usual quiet demeanor making him almost invisible in the corner.

Mike: “You two are seriously insane. How do you even come up with these experiments?”

Jolly: (quietly, to himself) “…they’re about to find out.”

The camera pans to the Bully, who sneaks in from the shadows. His smirk is almost predatory as he eyes the bubbling chemicals. His gloved hand hovers over one of the beakers, subtle and deliberate.

Scene 2 | Tampering and Tension
Interior – High School Science Lab – Continuous

The Bully tiptoes closer, deliberately misaligning a tube and replacing a harmless chemical with a volatile one from his backpack. The liquid shifts color subtly, from green to an ominous red. A faint crackle of energy escapes the mixture.

Monica: (noticing) “Wait… that’s not—”

Before she can finish, a loud pop echoes across the lab. Sparks fly. The green solution reacts violently with the red chemical. Smoke curls upward, thick and black, tinged with orange sparks.

Jack: (wide-eyed) “No… no, no! Step back!”

Jolly steps forward for the first time, his calm voice cutting through the chaos:

Jolly: “Time to shine.”

He presses a button on his device. A small pulse of energy emits from the machine, creating a protective barrier around the group just as the chemicals explode in a burst of fire and smoke. The lab is thrown into disarray. Shelves topple, glass shatters, and an eerie glow illuminates the terrified faces of the students.

Scene 3 | Zombies Emerge
Interior – Lab – Moments Later

The smoke clears. In the middle of the wreckage, zombie-like creatures begin to emerge. Their silhouettes are dark, twisted, and unfamiliar. Eyes glow faintly red through the smoke, and each movement is slow but deliberate.

Jennie, who had been watching from the doorway, gasps. Her shock is immediate, but a small, determined smile creeps onto her face. Sparks from the lingering chemical fire catch in her hair, giving her a fierce, almost mystical aura.

Jennie: (softly) “So… this is it.”

The zombies lurch forward. Mike freezes, unsure what to do. Jack and Monica scramble to gather what chemicals they can, trying desperately to reverse the reaction.

Jack: “We need containment! Now!”

Monica: (frantically) “The barrier! Jolly, can you—”

Jolly doesn’t answer. He’s already moving. Hands glowing faintly with controlled energy, he steps toward the nearest zombie. With a sudden pulse, the creature is knocked back, temporarily stunned.

Jolly: “Step aside.”

The others watch, a mixture of fear and awe, as Jolly takes control of the situation.

Scene 4 | The First Battle
Interior – Lab – Continuous

Sparks fly from broken electrical panels, mingling with the chemical smoke. Fire dances along the floorboards and spilled liquids. Jolly moves with precision, creating energy pulses to keep the zombies at bay.

Jack: (shouting over the chaos) “We need an exit!”

Monica: “No! If we just leave, they’ll escape into the school!”

The Bully, now panicked, trips over debris, his confidence gone. Mike grabs his arm.

Mike: “Get out of here!”

Jolly: (calmly, to the group) “We end this here… or we all lose.”

He channels another surge of energy. Fire and ash swirl around him as he strikes forward, knocking back three zombies. Sparks dance around the lab like a storm of embers. The team now has a momentary advantage, enough to regroup near the emergency exit.

Scene 5 | Strategic Retreat
Interior – Lab – Moments Later

The group retreats to a corner. Monica frantically mixes chemicals, trying to create a temporary seal or distraction.

Monica: “This should hold them… for a few minutes at least.”

Jack: “Good. That’ll give us time to figure out what’s happening. Why this is happening.”

Jennie steps forward, her eyes glowing faintly from the sparks still lingering in the air.

Jennie: “It’s not just random. Something caused this.”

Jolly: “Yes. And we’re going to find it. But first…”

He motions for the others to follow him.

Scene 6 | Outside the Lab
Exterior – School Courtyard – Night

Smoke escapes from the broken windows of the lab. The once-quiet courtyard is bathed in the orange glow of fire, shadows flickering across the walls. Zombies press against the temporary barrier of chemicals but cannot break through.

Mike: (breathing heavily) “I can’t believe that just happened…”

Jack: “Believe it. And get ready. This is just the beginning.”

Jolly surveys the courtyard, eyes narrowed. He senses a larger danger lurking beyond the lab, one that the group isn’t yet aware of.

Jennie: “So… what now?”

Jolly: (determined) “Now… we prepare. Because tomorrow… it’s going to get worse.”

Sparks from a broken lamp post scatter across the courtyard, illuminating their determined faces. The camera pans upward to the dark, cloudy sky, hinting at more chaos to come.

Scene 7 | Cliffhanger Ending
Exterior – School Rooftop – Night

From the rooftop, a shadowy figure watches the chaos below. A low, menacing laugh echoes through the night. The figure disappears into the darkness as the camera zooms in on the terrified but resolute group below.

